Chapter: CraftGump
  cites Uoaix chapter GamePackets

 The craft gump (UOAIX-185), after ServUO Engines/Craft CraftGump: a title, the categories down the left, the chosen
 category's items down the right with what each makes and needs, a status line, and Make Last and Exit. ServUO draws
 it with art the 1998 GUMPIDX lacks (5054, 4005-4012); this one uses the 2600 backing and the 15 by 15 round button
 2117 (pressed 2118), both in it. Each category is a gump page, so choosing one is the client's own page switch
 (button type 0); only an item, Make Last or Exit answers the server (0xB1). Every text and button lies inside the
 2600 frame (corners 47 by 44, left edge 34, right edge 45, bottom 40; UOAIX-230): x 52 to 485, y 52 to 440 of 530 by 480.
 Category names are ServUO's Def files' (DefBlacksmithy, DefTailoring, DefCarpentry, DefTinkering, DefCooking,
 DefBowFletching, DefAlchemy, DefInscription), in their order; a category with nothing in it is not shown.
  crg-tag : Integer = #43520000
  crg-make-last : Integer = 9999
 Alchemy and Inscription sit above the tool categories (gcr-category 1 to 9).
  crg-alchemy : Integer = 20
  crg-inscription : Integer = 21
  crg-labels : Integer -> List Text
  crg-labels (craft) = if craft == crg-alchemy then ["Healing and Curative", "Enhancement", "Toxic", "Explosive"]
    else if craft == crg-inscription then ["First Circle", "Second Circle", "Third Circle", "Fourth Circle", "Fifth Circle", "Sixth Circle", "Seventh Circle", "Eighth Circle"]
    else if craft == 1 then ["Metal Armor", "Helmets", "Shields", "Bladed", "Axes", "Polearms", "Bashing"]
    else if craft == 2 then ["Hats", "Shirts and Pants", "Miscellaneous", "Footwear", "Leather Armor", "Studded Armor", "Female Armor", "Bone Armor"]
    else if craft == 3 | (craft >= 7 & craft <= 9) then ["Other", "Furniture", "Containers", "Weapons", "Armor", "Instruments", "Misc", "Tailoring and Cooking", "Anvils and Forges", "Training"]
    else if craft == 4 then ["Wooden Items", "Tools", "Parts", "Utensils", "Miscellaneous", "Jewelry", "Multi-component Items", "Traps"]
    else if craft == 5 then ["Ingredients", "Preparations", "Baking", "Barbecue"]
    else if craft == 6 then ["Materials", "Ammunition", "Weapons"] else ["Items"]
 The category of a catalog item within a craft: dagger 69 and longsword 70 are Bladed, plate gorget 71 Metal Armor;
 shirt 72 and short pants 73 Shirts and Pants, footwear 121-124 Footwear; boards 38 and arrows 49 Other, furniture 47
 Furniture, bow 48 Weapons; the toolkits 42 and scissors 74 Tools, nails 39 Parts; bread 34 Baking, cooked meat and
 fish 50 Barbecue; for the fletcher, arrows Ammunition and the bow Weapons.
  crg-category : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  crg-category (craft) (item) = if craft == 1 then (if item == 69 | item == 70 then 3 else 0)
    else if craft == 2 then (if item == 72 | item == 73 then 1 else if item >= 121 & item <= 124 then 3 else 2)
    else if craft == 3 | (craft >= 7 & craft <= 9) then (if item == 47 | (item >= 128 & item <= 133) then 1 else if item >= 134 & item <= 138 then 2 else if item == 48 | item == 77 then 3
      else if item >= 139 & item <= 142 then 5 else if item == 143 then 6 else if item == 144 | item == 145 | item == 147 then 7 else if item == 146 then 9 else 0)
    else if craft == 4 then (if item == 42 | item == 74 then 1 else if item == 39 | item == 148 then 2 else 4)
    else if craft == 5 then (if item == 34 then 2 else if item == 50 then 3 else 1)
    else if craft == 6 then (if item == 49 then 1 else if item == 48 then 2 else 0) else 0
  crg-ucs2 : List Integer, Text, Integer -> List Integer
  crg-ucs2 (bytes) (text) (i) = if i >= text-length text then bytes
    else crg-ucs2 (gp-put16 bytes (to-unicode (char-code (char-at text i)))) text (i + 1)
  crg-lines : List Integer, List Text, Integer -> List Integer
  crg-lines (bytes) (texts) (i) = if i >= list-length texts then bytes
    else let t = list-at texts i in crg-lines (crg-ucs2 (gp-put16 bytes (text-length t)) t 0) texts (i + 1)
  crg-has : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  crg-has (cats) (k) (i) = if i >= list-length cats then False else if list-at cats i == k then True else crg-has cats k (i + 1)
 The categories that hold an item, in label order.
  crg-used : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  crg-used (cats) (count) (k) (out) = if k >= count then out else crg-used cats count (k + 1) (if crg-has cats k 0 then out & [k] else out)
  crg-left : List Text, List Integer, Integer, Text, List Text -> Text
  crg-left (labels) (used) (j) (layout) (texts) = if j >= list-length used then layout
    else let y = 108 + 22 * j
    in crg-left labels used (j + 1) (layout & "{ button 52 " & show y & " 2117 2118 0 " & show (j + 1) & " 0 }{ text 72 " & show (y - 2) & " 0 " & show (list-length texts + j) & " }") texts
  crg-left-texts : List Text, List Integer, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  crg-left-texts (labels) (used) (j) (out) = if j >= list-length used then out else crg-left-texts labels used (j + 1) (out & [list-at labels (list-at used j)])
 One page a category: a round button answering the item's id (its place in the menu, from 1, unless the menu gives
 ids) and its line.
  crg-page : List Text, List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text, List Text -> Text
  crg-page (names) (cats) (ids) (k) (i) (row) (layout) (texts) = if i >= list-length names | row >= 13 then layout
    else if list-at cats i /= k then crg-page names cats ids k (i + 1) row layout texts
    else let y = 108 + 22 * row
    in crg-page names cats ids k (i + 1) (row + 1) (layout & "{ button 250 " & show y & " 2117 2118 1 0 " & show (list-at ids i) & " }{ text 270 " & show (y - 2) & " 0 " & show (list-length texts + row) & " }") texts
  crg-page-texts : List Text, List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  crg-page-texts (names) (cats) (k) (i) (out) = if i >= list-length names then out
    else crg-page-texts names cats k (i + 1) (if list-at cats i == k then out & [list-at names i] else out)
  crg-pages : List Text, List Integer, List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Text, List Text -> List Text
  crg-pages (names) (cats) (ids) (used) (j) (layout) (texts) = if j >= list-length used then [layout] & texts
    else let k = list-at used j
    in let page = crg-page names cats ids k 0 0 (layout & "{ page " & show (j + 1) & " }") texts
    in crg-pages names cats ids used (j + 1) page (crg-page-texts names cats k 0 texts)
 The gump packet: names and cats are the menu's items in choice order and each one's category in labels; ids are the
 buttons' answers, and Make Last shows only when lastable.
  crg-gump : Integer, Integer, Text, List Text, List Text, List Integer, Text -> List Integer
  crg-gump (serial) (context) (title) (labels) (names) (cats) (status) = crg-gump-ids serial context title labels names cats (crg-count (list-length names) 1 []) status True
  crg-count : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  crg-count (n) (i) (out) = if i > n then out else crg-count n (i + 1) (out & [i])
  crg-gump-ids : Integer, Integer, Text, List Text, List Text, List Integer, List Integer, Text, Boolean -> List Integer
  crg-gump-ids (serial) (context) (title) (labels) (names) (cats) (ids) (status) (lastable) =
    let used = crg-used cats (list-length labels) 0 []
    in let head-texts = [title & " Menu", "CATEGORIES", "SELECTIONS", (if status == "" then " " else status), "MAKE LAST", "EXIT"]
    in let head = "{ page 0 }{ resizepic 0 0 2600 530 480 }{ text 200 52 0 0 }{ text 52 80 0 1 }{ text 250 80 0 2 }{ text 52 395 0 3 }"
      & (if lastable then "{ button 52 422 2117 2118 1 0 " & show crg-make-last & " }{ text 72 420 0 4 }" else "") & "{ button 400 422 2117 2118 1 0 0 }{ text 420 420 0 5 }"
    in let left = crg-left labels used 0 head head-texts
    in let texts = crg-left-texts labels used 0 head-texts
    in let built = crg-pages names cats ids used 0 left texts
    in let layout = list-at built 0
    in let lines = crg-rest built 1 []
    in let start = gp-put16 (gp-put32 (gp-put32 (gp-put32 (gp-put32 ((gp-start #B0) & [0, 0]) serial) (crg-tag + context)) 60) 60) (text-length layout + 1)
    in let counted = gp-put16 (gp-ascii start layout 0 (text-length layout + 1)) (list-length lines)
    in crg-finish (crg-lines counted lines 0)
  crg-rest : List Text, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  crg-rest (xs) (i) (out) = if i >= list-length xs then out else crg-rest xs (i + 1) (out & [list-at xs i])
  crg-finish : List Integer -> List Integer
  crg-finish (p) = let a = list-set-at p 1 (bit-and (bit-shr (list-length p) 8) 255) in let b = list-set-at p 2 (bit-and (list-length p) 255) in p
 A craft gump's answer (0xB1: serial at 3, gump id at 7, button at 11) becomes the 13-byte 0x7D menu choice the craft
 handler takes: the tool, the menu context, the choice (Make Last's 9999 included); button 0 (Exit, or a right click)
 is choice 0, which cancels. Any other packet passes through unchanged.
  crg-answer : List Integer -> List Integer
  crg-answer (packet) = if list-length packet < 15 | list-at packet 0 /= #B1 | bit-and (gp-u32 packet 7) #FFFF0000 /= crg-tag then packet
    else gp-put16 (gp-put16 (gp-put16 (gp-put32 [#7D] (gp-u32 packet 3)) (bit-and (gp-u32 packet 7) #FFFF)) (gp-u32 packet 11)) 0 & [0, 0]
